Paninda revision 006 — offline session retention and unreachable-file status
Date: 2026-11-05 (UTC)
Branch: litmus_2
Base: 55d4986

REQUEST / ROOT CAUSE
Internet loss must preserve offline work and show an offline X on Sync Status.
An inaccessible workbook must show sync failure, not send the user to onboarding.
The prior connected-app error path displayed ConnectionNoticeScreen and hid the
normal app/navigation after sync errors. That onboarding-style screen was wrong
for an already-connected local session; repository binding writes were separate.

IMPLEMENTED
- Removed the connected app's full-screen onboarding-style cloud error path.
  Sync failure opens/stays on the normal Sync Status route with bottom navigation
  and a brief snackbar. Disconnect failure stays in the app and reports that the
  grant/session were not removed. Initial setup errors retain their setup screen.
- Added domain NetworkStatus and data/network/NetworkMonitor. Android default-
  network callbacks observe validated internet separately from the persisted
  Google/file binding. Wi-Fi without validated internet is treated as offline.
  Register before sampling initial state; unregister when observation ends.
  API 24–25 have an asynchronous capability-sampling compatibility fallback.
- ViewModel combines Room state with live network status. Internet loss never
  changes the saved connection flag, file ID/account, outbox or business records.
  The user can stay on any page and continue local work while offline.
- Shared sync getter adds OFFLINE and UNREACHABLE phases. Offline has precedence
  over an old success/busy label; lastSuccessfulAt remains unchanged. Returning
  online after a failed offline attempt shows Ready/Pending until a successful
  manual retry. Existing manual-sync behavior is retained; no background worker.
- Offline Sync Now fails before Google authorization/client resolution. Failures
  are classified independently: no internet, inaccessible file (403/404), network
  timeout/server transport failure, expired authorization, conflict and format.
  Failed requests update status only and preserve session/data/pending changes.
- Unreachable/deleted/permission-denied file: Sync failed with an X and a useful
  explanation/retry. Authorization errors offer retry/re-authorization inside the
  app. Conflict/contract issues continue to show their existing guidance.
- Figma 19:305 supplies the Sync Status layout, serif status headline, condensed
  body and Sync Now card. Existing Material components/palette reused. The user's
  explicit offline X overrides the reference's warning triangle. Successful sync
  still uses the checkmark from revision 005. Home keeps its last-sync subtitle.
- First-time connection still needs internet. Only successful explicit Settings
  disconnect/revocation returns an established session to onboarding.

VERIFICATION
- Extended the existing behavior smoke check: validated internet/synced status,
  connection lost/offline X, Sync Now without onboarding, then Home/Inventory and
  local product creation/persistence. This exercises production network callbacks
  and the real offline preflight without Google/network calls.
- Existing repository check now verifies offline/unreachable/access/failed states
  retain the binding, last success, local products and pending changes before an
  explicit disconnect. Extended getter coverage and added one failure-policy test.
- No maintained layout tests, screenshot baselines or device matrix added.
  Temporary ignored renders inspect only the requested Sync Status component.
- Build/test/lint and render inspection outcomes are appended after completion.
- Physical device Wi-Fi/mobile transitions and real Google file-access failures
  still need acceptance on the user's device; no live-device claim is made.

FINAL CHECKS
- assembleDebug + lintDebug succeeded. Android lint: 0 errors.
- All 19 maintained regression checks passed (0 failures/errors). The expanded
  behavior smoke check proves Sync Now offline stays in the app and still allows
  local product creation, navigation and persistence through activity recreation.
- Temporary render inspection passed for offline X, unreachable-file X and success
  checkmark states. Existing metadata/pending rows remain; no unrelated layout
  changes were made. The render harness/images stay ignored under work/.
- Network-monitor observation failures fall back to Unknown rather than breaking
  Room loading or closing the saved local session.
- APK: app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk. No remote Git push or Drive
  upload requested in this correction turn; changes are committed locally.
